{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-23905","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-28090","text":"TRVM conformance"}]},{"id":"blk-23906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28091","text":"How a new implementation of the TRVM runtime proves it is correct. This is the contract "},{"id":"spn-28092","marks":["code"],"text":"spec/SPEC.md §6"},{"id":"spn-28093","text":" defines, made executable."}]},{"id":"blk-23907","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-28094","text":"What an implementation must do"}]},{"id":"blk-23908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28095","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-28096","marks":["bold"],"text":"Reproduce every vector."},{"id":"spn-28097","text":" "},{"id":"spn-28098","marks":["code"],"text":"vectors/normalize.json"},{"id":"spn-28099","text":" is a list of "},{"id":"spn-28100","marks":["code"],"text":"{ term, nf, ref_interactions }"},{"id":"spn-28101","text":". Each "},{"id":"spn-28102","marks":["code"],"text":"term"},{"id":"spn-28103","text":" is in the surface IC/lambda syntax ("},{"id":"spn-28104","marks":["code"],"text":"λ"},{"id":"spn-28105","text":", application "},{"id":"spn-28106","marks":["code"],"text":"(f x)"},{"id":"spn-28107","text":", superposition "},{"id":"spn-28108","marks":["code"],"text":"&L{a,b}"},{"id":"spn-28109","text":", duplication "},{"id":"spn-28110","marks":["code"],"text":"!&L{a,b}=v; body"},{"id":"spn-28111","text":", eraser "},{"id":"spn-28112","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-28113","text":"). Your runtime MUST normalize "},{"id":"spn-28114","marks":["code"],"text":"term"},{"id":"spn-28115","text":" to exactly "},{"id":"spn-28116","marks":["code"],"text":"nf"},{"id":"spn-28117","text":" (canonical naming: bound variables renamed "},{"id":"spn-28118","marks":["code"],"text":"a, b, c, …"},{"id":"spn-28119","text":" in first-encounter order; free names preserved). "},{"id":"spn-28120","marks":["code"],"text":"ref_interactions"},{"id":"spn-28121","text":" is the Python reference reducer's interaction count — a *native/optimal-sharing* runtime may take a different number of interactions, so only the "},{"id":"spn-28122","marks":["bold"],"text":"normal form"},{"id":"spn-28123","text":" is normative across runtimes; the interaction count is pinned only for the reference reducer it was recorded from."}]},{"id":"blk-23909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28124","text":"The vectors are "},{"id":"spn-28125","marks":["bold"],"text":"cross-validated at authoring time"},{"id":"spn-28126","text":": a term is only included if "},{"id":"spn-28127","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_float"},{"id":"spn-28128","text":" (Python reference) and "},{"id":"spn-28129","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-28130","text":" (C) already agree on its normal form, so you can diff against "},{"id":"spn-28131","marks":["code"],"text":"nf"},{"id":"spn-28132","text":" directly."}]},{"id":"blk-23910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28133","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-28134","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pass the behavioral batteries"},{"id":"spn-28135","text":" (SPEC §6.1–§6.3):"}]},{"id":"blk-23911","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23913","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28136","marks":["bold"],"text":"§6.1 Confluence"},{"id":"spn-28137","text":" — for a battery of nets, N random reduction orders MUST yield"}]}],"id":"blk-23912","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23914","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28138","text":"the identical normal form *and* identical interaction count."}]},{"id":"blk-23915","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28139","marks":["bold"],"text":"§6.2 Distributed == sequential"},{"id":"spn-28140","text":" — reduction under random partitions and random"}]}],"id":"blk-23916","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28141","text":"message-delivery order MUST match the single-node normal form and interaction count."}]},{"id":"blk-23919","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-23921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28142","marks":["bold"],"text":"§6.3 Exactly-once boundary"},{"id":"spn-28143","text":" — boundary exports MUST equal boundary rewrites in"}]}],"id":"blk-23920","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-23922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28144","text":"every run."}]},{"id":"blk-23923","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-28145","text":"Coverage status (honest)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23925","spans":[{"id":"spn-28146","text":"Check"}]},{"id":"blk-23926","spans":[{"id":"spn-28147","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-23927","spans":[{"id":"spn-28148","text":"Where it runs"}]}],"id":"blk-23924","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23928","spans":[{"id":"spn-28149","text":"Cross-runtime normal-form vectors"}]},{"id":"blk-23929","spans":[{"id":"spn-28150","marks":["bold"],"text":"covered"}]},{"id":"blk-23930","spans":[{"id":"spn-28151","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/python/conformance.py"},{"id":"spn-28152","text":" — 6 runtimes: "},{"id":"spn-28153","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_float"},{"id":"spn-28154","text":", "},{"id":"spn-28155","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-28156","text":", "},{"id":"spn-28157","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-28158","text":" (C), "},{"id":"spn-28159","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32.wasm"},{"id":"spn-28160","text":", "},{"id":"spn-28161","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32z"},{"id":"spn-28162","text":" (Zig), "},{"id":"spn-28163","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32m"},{"id":"spn-28164","text":" (Mojo)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23931","spans":[{"id":"spn-28165","text":"§6.1 confluence (300 random orders)"}]},{"id":"blk-23932","spans":[{"id":"spn-28166","marks":["bold"],"text":"covered"}]},{"id":"blk-23933","spans":[{"id":"spn-28167","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/python/inet.py"},{"id":"spn-28168","text":" battery"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23934","spans":[{"id":"spn-28169","text":"§6.2 distributed == sequential"}]},{"id":"blk-23935","spans":[{"id":"spn-28170","marks":["bold"],"text":"covered"}]},{"id":"blk-23936","spans":[{"id":"spn-28171","marks":["code"],"text":"distribution/dist_ic.py"},{"id":"spn-28172","text":" (480 runs)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23937","spans":[{"id":"spn-28173","text":"§6.3 exactly-once boundary"}]},{"id":"blk-23938","spans":[{"id":"spn-28174","marks":["bold"],"text":"covered"}]},{"id":"blk-23939","spans":[{"id":"spn-28175","marks":["code"],"text":"inet.py"},{"id":"spn-28176","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-28177","marks":["code"],"text":"dist_ic.py"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23940","spans":[{"id":"spn-28178","text":"§6.4 snapshot round-trip"}]},{"id":"blk-23941","spans":[{"id":"spn-28179","marks":["bold"],"text":"GAP"}]},{"id":"blk-23942","spans":[{"id":"spn-28180","text":"no "},{"id":"spn-28181","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot()"},{"id":"spn-28182","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-28183","marks":["code"],"text":"restore()"},{"id":"spn-28184","text":" in the reference yet"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23943","spans":[{"id":"spn-28185","text":"§6.5 REF unfolding"}]},{"id":"blk-23944","spans":[{"id":"spn-28186","marks":["bold"],"text":"GAP"}]},{"id":"blk-23945","spans":[{"id":"spn-28187","text":"recursive supercombinator REFs not exercised"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28188","text":"The two gaps are intentional and tracked — see "},{"id":"spn-28189","marks":["code"],"text":"FINDINGS.md"},{"id":"spn-28190","text":" \"Honest limits / standing gaps\". Do not claim full §6 conformance until they are wired."}]},{"id":"blk-23947","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-28191","text":"Running it"}]},{"id":"blk-23948","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"make test                              # everything below\npython3 runtime/python/conformance.py  # just the conformance runner"},{"id":"blk-23949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28192","text":"The runner auto-detects which backends are present. It always checks the Python reference; it additionally checks any of the following that exist:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-23951","spans":[{"id":"spn-28193","text":"Backend"}]},{"id":"blk-23952","spans":[{"id":"spn-28194","text":"Built by"}]},{"id":"blk-23953","spans":[{"id":"spn-28195","text":"Binary"}]}],"id":"blk-23950","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-23954","spans":[{"id":"spn-28196","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-28197","text":" (C)"}]},{"id":"blk-23955","spans":[{"id":"spn-28198","marks":["code"],"text":"make native"}]},{"id":"blk-23956","spans":[{"id":"spn-28199","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/c/ic32"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23957","spans":[{"id":"spn-28200","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32.wasm"}]},{"id":"blk-23958","spans":[{"id":"spn-28201","text":"prebuilt; needs "},{"id":"spn-28202","marks":["code"],"text":"node"}]},{"id":"blk-23959","spans":[{"id":"spn-28203","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/wasm/ic32.wasm"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23960","spans":[{"id":"spn-28204","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32(zig)"}]},{"id":"blk-23961","spans":[{"id":"spn-28205","marks":["code"],"text":"make zig"}]},{"id":"blk-23962","spans":[{"id":"spn-28206","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/zig/ic32z"}]}],[{"id":"blk-23963","spans":[{"id":"spn-28207","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32(mojo)"}]},{"id":"blk-23964","spans":[{"id":"spn-28208","marks":["code"],"text":"make mojo"}]},{"id":"blk-23965","spans":[{"id":"spn-28209","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/mojo/ic32m"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-23966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28210","text":"A backend that is "},{"id":"spn-28211","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-28212","text":" built is reported as *skipped*, with a note naming the missing path — never silently treated as passing. This matters more than it looks: \"0 failures\" from a runner that checked nothing is precisely the failure mode a conformance suite exists to prevent, so an unbuilt backend must be visible rather than invisible. The same applies to the Zig and Mojo "},{"id":"spn-28213","marks":["code"],"text":"make"},{"id":"spn-28214","text":" targets, which skip (not fail) when their toolchain is absent, so the battery still runs end-to-end on a machine that has only a C compiler."}]},{"id":"blk-23967","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28215","text":"Because only the normal form is normative (§1 above), the runner asserts "},{"id":"spn-28216","marks":["bold"],"text":"NF agreement"},{"id":"spn-28217","text":" for every backend but pins "},{"id":"spn-28218","marks":["code"],"text":"ref_interactions"},{"id":"spn-28219","text":" to "},{"id":"spn-28220","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_float"},{"id":"spn-28221","text":" alone."}]},{"id":"blk-23968","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-28222","text":"Adding vectors"}]},{"id":"blk-23969","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-28223","text":"Regenerate / extend by running candidate terms through *both* the Python reference and the native runtime and keeping only those where they agree — that invariant is what makes the file safe to diff against from any language. Keep terms within the labeling discipline interaction-net reduction requires (linear binders, distinct fan labels for independent duplicators); naively-shared labels reduce incorrectly *by design* and are not valid vectors."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieratg5t26hnv4wyvmsxblbvzbb3ytqfqbbsgvcrptegcdi6yywiodwa","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}